From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:14:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sb/intel/lynxpoint: Drop the GPIO ASL that no board uses

pch.asl includes the common GPIO level methods (GRXS, GTXS, STXS, CTXS),
with an OperationRegion over the whole GPIO I/O space, 0x480-0x4eb. No
Lynx Point mainboard calls them. Linux, when lpc_ich claims the GPIO I/O
ranges for gpio_ich, finds them inside that region and logs three

  ACPI Warning: SystemIO range 0x4C0-0x4CF conflicts with OpRegion
  0x480-0x4EB (\_SB.PCI0.GPLV)
  ACPI: OSL: Resource conflict; ACPI support missing from driver?

at every boot, and does not register gpio_ich. Drop the include; the
Lynx Point-LP boards have their own gpio.asl in lpc.asl, untouched.

TEST=ThinkPad W541: the DSDT compiles without the region.

Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/acpi/pch.asl | 5 -----
 1 file changed, 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/acpi/pch.asl b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/acpi/pch.asl
index 256147fa..c8492eaf 100644
--- a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/acpi/pch.asl
+++ b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/acpi/pch.asl
@@ -48,11 +48,6 @@ Scope (\)
 #endif
 }
 
-#if !CONFIG(INTEL_LYNXPOINT_LP)
-// General purpose GPIO access methods
-#include <southbridge/intel/common/acpi/gpio.asl>
-#endif
-
 // High Definition Audio (Azalia) 0:1b.0
 #include "audio.asl"
 
